  "text": "In February 2013 we returned most to the same words at once around one occasion. Twenty-three of us said \"state of the union\" by 2013-02-12, and twenty of us said \"state of the union address\" that same day; John Barrasso first said the former, Tim Walberg the latter. Eight of us reached \"require a plan act\" on 2013-02-06, first said by Charles J. \"Chuck\" Fleischmann, and seven of us said \"the require a plan act.\" Nine of us said \"violence against women\" and eight \"violence against women act\" by 2013-02-28. Seven of us said \"children and grandchildren,\" and seven said \"secretary of defense\" by 2013-02-26. These are the phrases we repeated together, and the counts of us who repeated them. We record them here as our own convergence, without adding to what the record shows.",
